# Local Worker secrets, read by `wrangler dev` at startup. Copy this file to
# `cloud/.dev.vars` (gitignored) and fill in as needed. Production secrets are
# set out-of-band via `wrangler secret put`, never from this file.
#
# After editing cloud/.dev.vars, restart `./per-ankh dev` — wrangler only reads
# it at startup.

# Enables the Discord-free dev-login bypass (GET /v1/auth/dev/login), the
# recommended way to get a local session. Local-only: the handler 404s unless
# this is set AND the request is non-HTTPS, so it stays dark in prod. Full usage
# in docs/dev-login.md.
#
# It also gates GET /v1/dev/images/*, which serves uploaded screenshots out of
# the local R2 bucket — production serves those from an R2 custom domain with no
# Worker in the path, so without this route the galleries render 404s locally.
# `./per-ankh dev` points SCREENSHOT_BASE_URL at it; nothing else to set.
DEV_LOGIN=1

# Shared key that lets this Worker believe the visitor IP the frontend Worker
# forwards on server-rendered requests (cloud/src/util.ts
# adoptTrustedFrontend). The value below matches SSR_TRUSTED_KEY in the
# committed `.env.development`, so copying this file as-is exercises the same
# path locally that prod uses; leaving it out just means SSR requests count
# against the dev server's own address, as they did before forwarding existed.
# In prod/staging it's a real secret, set on BOTH Workers:
#   npx wrangler secret put SSR_TRUSTED_KEY            (this Worker)
#   npx wrangler secret put SSR_TRUSTED_KEY --config ../wrangler.toml
SSR_TRUSTED_KEY=dev-ssr-trusted-key

# Only needed for REAL Discord OAuth locally (skip it if you use DEV_LOGIN
# above). Get the value from the Discord app at
# https://discord.com/developers/applications. Real OAuth also requires that app
# to register http://localhost:1420/auth/callback as a redirect URI.
DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional: unlocks site-admin actions locally (e.g. bulk reparse). isSiteAdmin
# (cloud/src/admin.ts) matches the logged-in user's discord_id against this, so
# set it to the discord_id you log in as.
ADMIN_DISCORD_ID=

# Optional: YouTube Data API key, used only to resolve an @handle or /user/ URL
# to its channel id when a user links a channel (cloud/src/video/youtube.ts).
# A …/channel/UC… URL resolves without it, and fetching recent videos never
# needs it (unauthenticated RSS). Get a key from the Google Cloud console
# (enable "YouTube Data API v3"). In prod/staging set it out-of-band:
#   npx wrangler secret put YOUTUBE_API_KEY   (and again with --env staging)
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# Optional: bearer token for `./per-ankh admin reparse-all --local`, the
# headless reparse sweep. It has no session, so POST
# /v1/admin/games/:user_id/reparse-upload accepts this instead
# (siteAdminFromCliToken, cloud/src/admin.ts); no other admin route does.
# The sweep reads this same file when targeting --local, so the value below
# is all there is to set — but ADMIN_DISCORD_ID above must also be set, and
# you must have logged in as it once, since the audit row names that user.
# In prod/staging it's a real secret:
#   npx wrangler secret put ADMIN_CLI_TOKEN   (and again with --env staging)
ADMIN_CLI_TOKEN=dev-admin-cli-token
